        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Ghostkeeper, Lonesome Dove: The Series\n- Concepts: Windigo legend, Wendigo psychosis\n- People: Georgie Collins\n- Topics: North American folklore, culture-bound syndromes\n\nFacts:\n- The 1981 cult horror film Ghostkeeper has a plot inspired by the Windigo legend of North America.\n- Georgie Collins is known for her role in the 1981 cult horror film Ghostkeeper.\n- Georgie Collins is also known for her part in Lonesome Dove: The Series (1995).\n- The Wendigo legend gave its name to the modern medical term Wendigo psychosis.\n- Psychiatrists have described Wendigo psychosis as a controversial culture-bound syndrome marked by symptoms such as an intense craving for human flesh and a fear of becoming a cannibal.",
